The '''Padmanabhaswamy Temple''' ({{IPA|ml|pɐd̪mɐnaːbʰɐswaːmi|lang}}) is a [[Hindu temple]] dedicated to [[Vishnu]] in [[Thiruvananthapuram]], [[Kerala]], India. It is one of the 108 [[Divya Desam]]s which are considered the sacred sites of the [[Sri Vaishnavism|Sri Vaishnava]] tradition.

The temple's principal deity is [[Anantha Padmanabhaswamy]], a form of Vishnu depicted in [[Yoga-nidra|yogic sleep]], on his serpent mount named [[Shesha]]. Padmanabhaswamy is the [[tutelary deity]] of the [[Travancore royal family]]. The titular [[Maharaja of Travancore]], [[Moolam Thirunal Rama Varma]], is the current trustee of the temple.

